{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Debug report — fix pushed as Gerrit change 1983\n\n### Proven root cause\n\nDecorate-then-fit ordering. `_decorate_outbound_comment` (`outbound_comments.py:205`)\nputs `RECONCILER_MARKER` at the very END of the body; every vendor fitter truncates\nfrom the RIGHT. The one live Cloud comment send path\n(`adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py:531`, `codec.to_wire(codec.fit_outbound(body))`)\nreceived the already-decorated body, so the marker was always the first thing cut.\n\n### Proof (runtime, discriminating)\n\n- A 40,000-char decorated body fits to 31,887 chars ending in the truncation notice\n  with NO marker; a short body keeps it -> the loss is length-triggered.\n- All four fitters drop it (plain ADF, rich ADF, `truncate_comment_body`, DC wiki),\n  which rules out \"one bad fitter\" and identifies the ORDERING as the defect.\n- Feeding the landed wire back through the inbound predicate: short -> `True`,\n  over-length -> `False`. The loop-breaker is provably inert.\n- `truncate_comment_body` output is exactly 32767 chars ending in\n  `\" … [truncated by reconciler]\"` — byte-identical to the 836 live duplicates,\n  dating the damage to the pre-ADF-encode plaintext send path.\n\n### The fix and its ordering rationale\n\n`fit_preserving_marker(text, fit)` in `outbound_comments.py`, called from\n`acli_cli_ops.add_comment`. It truncates the CONTENT and re-appends the decoration,\nso the marker sits INSIDE the budget instead of hanging off its end — the reservation\nthe AC asked for, expressed as a re-ordering rather than as edits to four fitters.\n\nWhy here and not in the fitters: the fitters are shared with descriptions, which\ncarry no marker, and `jira_family` may not import `adapters/jira`. Making each\nfitter marker-aware would have added a fourth copy of the marker literal and a\nfourth of the truncation-notice literal. Instead the fitter is INJECTED as\n`Callable[[str], str]`, so this backend-neutral core module still names no vendor\nand no numeric limit (`test_backend_neutrality.py` passes), and the vendor's notice\nis DERIVED from a single probe of `fit` rather than restated.\n\nBehaviour: text not ending in the marker goes straight to `fit` (byte-identical —\nverified); a decorated body already within the limit is returned untouched; an\nover-limit one is rebuilt by binary-searching the largest content prefix whose\ndecorated form is a fixed point of `fit`.\n\nConstraints checked: `_normalize_comment_body` still strips the marker, and the\ndedup key is identical with and without it. Marker detection stays PRE-STRIP on the\nrendered text — the inbound predicate now returns `True` for over-length echoes.\n\nRobustness sweep: 70 combinations (5 body shapes x 7 lengths x rich/plain), zero\nfailures on all five postconditions plus idempotence.\n\n### Would existing marker-less comments be re-posted? NO — verified, not assumed\n\nThe fix changes only what is POSTED; no comparison or dedup key changes. Running the\ndiffer against a legacy marker-less landed body BEFORE and AFTER the fix gives an\nidentical result, so the change induces no re-post and needs no migration.\n\nSeparately: that body-equality path already misses for over-length comments today\n(local key 32767 chars vs landed 31887) because the differ fits at\n`_JIRA_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS` while the send path fits at the 32000 ADF limit. Filed as\n`abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey` (e339-9709-15fe-419a). In production the ID-based primary\nskip suppresses it.\n\n### RED -> GREEN and mutation\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py`\n— 5 tests at the observable send seam (the captured `--body` argument), including the\ncase that is over-limit only because the decoration pushed it over.\n\n- RED first: 4 failed / 1 passed (the in-limit regression guard), each failing on the\n  missing marker — the right reason.\n- Held out: physically moved out of the tree before the implementation subagent ran;\n  it never saw the file. GREEN on restore: 5 passed.\n- Mutation 1 (re-introduce the exact root cause — restore `codec.fit_outbound(body)`):\n  back to 4 failed. Mutation 2 (`notice = \"\"`): the truncation-notice test alone fails.\n  The test has teeth on both axes.\n- Refactoring litmus: assertions are on the emitted payload and decoded text only, no\n  private names or source greps.\n\n### Defect origin: UNATTRIBUTABLE (close class `preexisting`)\n\nDate test applied. Both implicated sites blame (`-w -C -M`) to `b534f47a7f`\n(2026-06-08), the DSO->rebar import commit whose parent holds only `README.md`. No\n`rebar-ticket:` trailer. The marker (DSO bug 85a1) and the truncation (DSO bug 6afc)\narrived together, so no later change broke working behaviour. `rebar show` for both\nDSO ids returns `ticket_not_found`; `git log -S` on all three symbols bottoms out at\nthe same import. Explicitly NOT charged to `27b868ba55` / emersed-specific-mutt: the\n32767-char production evidence predates it.\n\n### Scope, safety, siblings\n\n- Caller sweep: `add_comment` has one enactment site\n  (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:384`); no caller depends on the marker being absent or on\n  the truncated length. Incidental only.\n- Restoration, not creation: no new entry point, no new dependency, no test weakened.\n- Construct sweep: no other trailing token is appended after content and then fitted.\n- Parity census — CLI: N/A. MCP/API: N/A. Library facade: N/A. Automated callers: both\n  producers (`_diff_comments`, `_map_comments_for_create`) funnel through the one fixed\n  site. Dual-direction: inbound has no fit. Backends: Cloud fixed; DC applies NO fit on\n  the comment send path at all, so it cannot drop the marker — but its `sanitize_comment`\n  has no production caller, filed as `community-sediment-snipe` (b9b4-f460-2d54-4872).\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` green (ratchet `active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`); `make typecheck`\n`Success: no issues found in 613 source files`; full unit sweep **11942 passed, 44\nskipped, 0 failures** (includes the repo-wide oracles).\n\n### Replication\n\nThrough the real entry point with the report's own shape (40,000-char body): `--body`\n32,000 chars (<= 32767), marker present, truncation notice present, inbound\nloop-breaker recognises it. The original report no longer reproduces. No live Jira was\ntouched at any point — all fixture/stub."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787297162696705001,"uuid":"f57ffb33-9231-46f5-8b84-c61d6b818bc3"}